  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: The sole completed experiment (config_001, rna_only/singleprofile/pca_n2000) yields ~48.5% accuracy, establishing a modest RNA-only baseline. The largest uncertainty is whether the image modality contributes meaningful signal at all, which directly determines whether the 36 multimodal configurations (configs 016-051) are worth pursuing. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image modality's standalone predictive power under the same singleprofile setting as the RNA baseline, enabling a clean modality comparison. Why this is the best next step: With 8 experiments remaining, knowing whether image features are competitive with or complementary to RNA features is the highest-leverage decision. If image accuracy approaches or exceeds RNA, multimodal fusion becomes a strong exploitation target; if it falls well short, I can redirect budget toward RNA encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment resolves the most consequential branch in the search tree."
}

